# Flink Session Windowing (Event Time)

## Purpose
Identify bursts of events separated by a gap (session windows) in Apache Flink using event time.

## Setup / Requirements
- Use Flink's Event Time (Watermarks) and session windows.
- DataStream API.

## Key APIs
- `WatermarkStrategy.forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration)`
- `assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(...)`
- `keyBy(...)`
- `window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Duration))`
- `aggregate(...)` or `process(...)`

## Usage Pattern
```java
WatermarkStrategy<MyEvent> wm = WatermarkStrategy
    .<MyEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofMinutes(1))
    .withTimestampAssigner((e, ts) -> e.eventTimeMicros / 1000L);

DataStream<MyEvent> stream = env
    .fromSource(source, wm, "events")
    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(wm);

DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> perSessionCounts = stream
    .keyBy(e -> e.jobId)
    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Duration.ofMinutes(10)))
    .aggregate(new AggregateFunction<MyEvent, Integer, Integer>() {
        public Integer createAccumulator() { return 0; }
        public Integer add(MyEvent v, Integer acc) { return acc + 1; }
        public Integer getResult(Integer acc) { return acc; }
        public Integer merge(Integer a, Integer b) { return a + b; }
    }, new ProcessWindowFunction<Integer, Tuple2<Long,Integer>, Long, TimeWindow>() {
        public void process(Long key, Context ctx, Iterable<Integer> in, Collector<Tuple2<Long,Integer>> out) {
            out.collect(Tuple2.of(key, in.iterator().next()));
        }
    });

DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> maxPerJob = perSessionCounts
    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)
    .reduce((a,b) -> a.f1 >= b.f1 ? a : b);
```

## Notes
- Use event time timestamps (microseconds -> milliseconds).
- Session gap of 10 minutes ends a stage after inactivity.
- Reduce per job to get the maximum session count.
EOF"}

