# Google Cluster Traces: Task & Job Events Schema

## Purpose
Implement POJOs for task/job events from the Google cluster-usage traces CSV files.

## Setup / Requirements
- Fields are CSV columns from the dataset.
- Timestamps are in microseconds.
- Use `long` for numeric ids/timestamps; `int` for small enums.

## Common Parsing Pattern
```java
static long parseLong(String[] parts, int idx) {
    if (idx >= parts.length) return -1L;
    String v = parts[idx];
    if (v == null || v.isEmpty()) return -1L;
    return Long.parseLong(v);
}

static int parseInt(String[] parts, int idx) {
    if (idx >= parts.length) return -1;
    String v = parts[idx];
    if (v == null || v.isEmpty()) return -1;
    return Integer.parseInt(v);
}
```

## Notes
- Task events include a `job_id`, `task_index`, `event_type`, and `timestamp`.
- Job events include `job_id`, `event_type`, and `timestamp`.
- Keep constructors + public fields or getters (Flink POJO rules).
EOF"}

